{{also|osten|östen|Östen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{m|de|Ost}} or {{der|de|goh|ostan}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*austrą}}, related to {{m|ine-pro|*ausos||dawn}}, compare {{cog|la|aurora}}, and {{cog|la|auster}}, which, probably due to a re-orientation, means "South".

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈɔstən/|/ˈɔstn̩/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Osten.ogg|Audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-Osten.ogg|Audio (Austria)}}
* {{rhymes|de|ɔstən|ɔstn̩}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m.sg}}

# [[East]]
# {{lb|de|only with definite article}} The territory of the former [[GDR]].
# {{lb|de|by extension}} {{non-gloss definition|anything that is Eastern, e.g. Eastern Europe, Asia}}<!--really a distinct definition?-->

